Setting IP addresses

nmcli connection show

Set the IP and Netmask (CIDR):
sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33" ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.100/24

Set the Gateway:
sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33" ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1

Set the DNS:
sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33" ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8"

Set method to Manual (Static):
sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33" ipv4.method manual

Restart the connection:
sudo nmcli connection up "ens33"

Check DNS:
resolvectl status


sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33" ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.100/24 ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1 ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8" && sudo nmcli connection up "ens33"

echo "nameserver 192.168.72.20" > /etc/resolv.conf

sudo nmcli connection modify "ens33": Targets the connection profile named "ens33".
ipv4.method manual: Sets the IP to Static (Manual).
ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.100/24: Sets the IP and CIDR netmask.
ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1: Sets the Gateway.
ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8": Sets the DNS server.
&&: This Linux operator runs the next command only if the previous one succeeded.
sudo nmcli connection up "ens33": Restarts the connection to apply the changes immediately.
